WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.668 --> 00:00:03.818
- A narwhal's horn is
actually an enlarged tooth

00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:05.651
and not a horn at all.

00:00:10.273 --> 00:00:13.058
And today, we're talking about narwhals,

00:00:13.058 --> 00:00:14.725
unicorns of the sea.

00:00:16.077 --> 00:00:16.994
Nice shirt.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.713
- Thanks.

00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:24.363
(light piano music)

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.581
- My grandfather, Jacques Cousteau,

00:00:27.582 --> 00:00:29.952
studied and explored the Earth's ocean.

00:00:29.952 --> 00:00:31.034
I do too.

00:00:31.034 --> 00:00:32.969
And our submarine is in arctic waters,

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:35.802
searching for the narwhal.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.889
(errr, errr, er, er)

00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:40.389
Oh, he's a beauty.

00:00:41.406 --> 00:00:44.089
Now, narwhals can grow
up to 17 feet in length,

00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:47.626
and their front tooth can
grow up to 10 feet in length.

00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:50.343
It's the only straight tusk in the world.

00:00:50.343 --> 00:00:53.995
But typically, these
are only found on males

00:00:53.995 --> 00:00:57.396
and are actually full of up
to 10 million nerve endings,

00:00:57.396 --> 00:01:00.497
helping the narwhal detect
pressure, salt levels

00:01:00.497 --> 00:01:03.690
and even temperature in the water.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.488
Here's an interesting fact,

00:01:05.488 --> 00:01:07.689
a narwhal tusk is flexible.

00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:10.090
It can bend about one
foot in any direction,

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.408
without breaking.

00:01:11.408 --> 00:01:12.641
It was originally thought that

00:01:12.641 --> 00:01:14.362
these tusks were for dueling.

00:01:14.362 --> 00:01:18.511
But a new theory suggests,
they're for attracting a mate.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:22.511
Narwhals don't migrate
like other whale species.

00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.602
They spend their entire
lives in icy, arctic waters

00:01:34.602 --> 00:01:37.019
hunting squid, fish and crab.

00:01:38.274 --> 00:01:39.991
If you want to see one live,

00:01:39.991 --> 00:01:41.689
you'll have to come up north

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:44.341
because narwhals don't
thrive in captivity.

00:01:44.341 --> 00:01:45.758
Rather, they die.

00:01:47.044 --> 00:01:50.377
Some animals, we humans just can't tame.

